ket will decide.  As an analogy, and because I like the 2A, Rogan is akin to the Glock and every upstart is compared thereto.  No matter what competitors do, old steady Glock just keeps on selling units just as I think Rogan will just keep attracting listeners.  \n\nAlmost all current Rogan listeners will continue to listen to Rogan, his audience will continue to expand steadily, however, listeners will likely just expand their podcast listening portfolio to include Burr and Smith.  \n\nI have been to two Burr live performances and been a fan for a long time of his comedy, his last performance you could tell he was dabbling in political commentary.  The comedy suffered.  His previous performance was great, the last one was ok, more forced laughter than real.\n\nRegarding Stephen A., his rants have been things of legend in the past.  Contrary to Burr, however, my interest in what he has to say politically has grown and I find myself agreeing with him more and more on different, selective things.  I don't have to agree with someone 100% or even close to 100% to find their perspective useful.  Often what seems a point of disagreement turns out to be more of a complementary perspective that simply expands the horizon instead of replaces it.  \n\nLet's see if what Cuomo says comes true.  Somehow, like the Glock, I see Rogan dominating the scene for a long time to come.  Doesn't mean others won't be major players but topping the established king of anything is infinitely easier said than done.  This I do know, it won't be Cuomo that does it.", 'entity_set': {'hashtags': [], 'symbols': [], 'urls': [], 'user_mentions': []}, 'richtext': {'richtext_tags': []}, 'media': {'inline_media': []}}}}, 'legacy': {'bookmark_count': 0, 'bookmarked': False, 'created_at': 'Fri Jan 03 23:54:01 +0000 2025', 'conversation_id_str': '1875317383826669805', 'display_text_range': [14, 286], 'entities': {'hashtags': [], 'symbols': [], 'timestamps': [], 'urls': [], 'user_mentions': [{'id_str': '691